messages.content:
Execute 'FGBR_OC.ipynb'.  Save the results in html format in ../results. For all the runs, disable the cell execution timeout and allow errors.
Questions:
{
  "q1": "Report the best test R^2 value for c = 1.0.",
  "q2": "Report the best test RMSE value for c = 1.0."
}

arguments.command:
cd /code && jupyter nbconvert --to notebook --execute FGBR_OC.ipynb --ExecutePreprocessor.timeout=-1 --ExecutePreprocessor.allow_errors=True --output FGBR_OC_executed.ipynb --output-dir /results >/tmp/nb.log 2>&1; cat /tmp/nb.log && python - <<'PY'
import nbformat, json
nb=nbformat.read('/results/FGBR_OC_executed.ipynb', as_version=4)
for i,c in enumerate(nb.cells):
    if c.cell_type=='code' and c.outputs:
        print('CELL',i)
        for out in c.outputs:
            if out.output_type=='stream':
                print(out.text)
            elif out.output_type=='execute_result':
                print(out['data'].get('text/plain',''))
PY

